failure_scenario:
Reproduced: `// TODO(on: date('2019-07-01'), to: 'me@x.com')` followed by `/* stray block
//   inner line
end of block */` yields `todo.comment == "ray block
//   inner line
end of block */
"` — the real TODO's dispatched message is silently corrupted with leaked raw source. A related variant truncates later continuation lines, and another spawns a bogus empty Todo when a standalone block comment contains an embedded `// TODO(`.
